{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And YHWH desired to crush him.</b> Like דִּבְּרוֹ (Genesis 37:4), from the heavy dagesh [pi'el] stem." "<b>הֶחֱלִי.</b> It comes with a heh-pattern [prefix] in the manner of alef, even though we find תַּחֲלֻאֶיהָ אֲשֶׁר חָלָה יְיָ בָהּ (Deuteronomy 29:22). And behold, He desired to crush him, to chastise us in exile." "<b>If you make his soul a guilt-offering.</b> That he confess and acknowledge, and the meaning is: if you make his soul his guilt before Him, HaShem will multiply his seed, and prolong his days, that he and his seed may see the salvation of HaShem. And the hint speaks of the generation that will return to HaShem at the time of the end, the coming of the Messiah." "<b>And the desire of YHWH will prosper in his hand.</b> The meaning concerns the Torah, that the nations will return to the religion of HaShem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:23.686156499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}